# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AaltoFlow suite -- one ignore file for all nine projects.
# Each project also keeps its own .gitignore; this is the shared backstop.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Virtual environments. NEVER commit these: they are rebuilt from
# pyproject.toml + uv.lock on any machine, they are huge, and on OneDrive they
# are the source of the `Access is denied (os error 5)` locking trouble.
# (uv.lock IS committed -- that is what makes installs reproducible.)
.venv/
venv/
.uv/

# Python bytecode and build/packaging leftovers
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Test + tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Runtime output: scan datasets, figures and logs produced by run_demo.py,
# the engine and the services. Data belongs in the lab archive, not in git.
out/
*.nc
*.log
*.csv

# ...except the spike results, which are small (58 KB) and are the recorded
# EVIDENCE that those QCoDeS experiments worked -- the memory cites them.
!spikes/**/*.nc

# Local machine state that should not follow the repo between PCs
# suite_local.json = this PC's port overrides, real/sim flags and remote
# services (written by the launcher, read by scan-core); .suite_cache = the last
# `describe` seen from each module.
suite_local.json
.suite_local.*.tmp
.suite_cache/
mission-control/profiles.json
mission-control/launcher.json
scan-core/suite_layouts.json

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# offline packages copied in by "Add module..." from module packs
wheelhouse/

# Personal working notes (Claude Code loads them; they stay private)
CLAUDE.local.md
